on-arrival: {!
// the party grows month by month in 1919; between the great clashes the state of siege eases
Q.repression -= 6; Q.militancy -= 2;
if (!Q.ultraleft_gone && Q.heidelberg_outcome == 0) { Q.ultraleft_satisfaction = Math.max(Q.ultraleft_satisfaction, 30); }
var g = Math.max(1.05, Math.min(1.35, 1.24 + Q.worker_support / 200 - Q.repression / 400));
for (var d of Q.districts) { Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= g; }
Q.constitution_adopted = 1;
Q.stability += 5;
RG.news('Ebert signs the Weimar constitution', 3);
!}

= The Weimar Constitution

The Assembly adopted the constitution by 262 votes to 75, and on 11 August Ebert signed it at Schwarzburg. Universal suffrage, proportional representation, a president elected by the people.

Two articles matter to us. Article 165 promises councils in the factories, which is all that is left of the councils of November. Article 48 lets the President suspend basic rights and send in the army whenever public order is threatened.

- @councils: Prepare our lists for the factory council elections.
- @expose: Print Article 48 under the heading "Noske's constitution".

@councils
